#adm/daemons/mailmesg.c
remain ({"ruby@eastern stories",})
mesg "BEGIN FORWARDED TEXT:Elon writes:> Title: problem with 20.21 ...> From:  Elon> Date:  Sun Dec 11> >  > We are having problem with 20.21 driver running a heavily modified> TMI-2 lib based on version 1.0.1. Everything works ok.. fixed the> type checking and stuff like that....> But the driver crashes often... it'll go like this:> first crash at around 6-8 hours of uptime, 2nd crash at about 2-3> minutes apart of 1st crash.. and 3rd crashes will occure about 5 min> after the 2nd.. then someone will be there to shut it down and restart> the mud.> we've found so far, is that the mud takes up a little bit more memory> compare to when we are running under 9.19 driver (about 2-3M) and when> there's 25 players on, the driver will have 10 hours of uptime before> crash, but with 40 people on, it crashes about 2 hr of uptime.> and all the crashes did not get logged into driver log or debug log> or mudlib log.. the only trace of crashes is on the UPRECORD file which> all have exit code 141 logged..>  > anybody has any idea what's going on?>  > -Elon.> > "
